    "id": 4891,
    "post": 547,
    "parent": 0,
    "author": 0,
    "author_name": "Devyone S Corley",
    "author_url": "",
    "date": "2018-12-07T00:00:39",
    "date_gmt": "2018-12-07T04:00:39",
    "content": {
      "rendered": "<p>Hi Pete,<br />\nGlad I read your post bc I would have been taken by surprised with my current accident case. My 7 year old daughter and I were involved in a accident on 9/17/2018. To make a long story short my car was totalled when a lady crashed into me from behind. We both went to the ER, I&#8217;ve done physical therapy and I&#8217;ve seen a neurologist. My daughter did not receive any treatment after the ER. I was told the policy limit on the accident claim is 100/300. I was told the most I can recover is 100k and the same for my daughter. My question is do I need to be looking at options of a structured settlement? Can you speak with me in private via email or text maybe?</p>\n"
    },
    "link": "https://kidinjurylaw.com/2022/07/15/legal-strategies-to-minimize-or-avoid-court-involvement-in-georgia-child-injury-settlements-part-i/#comment-4891",
