  {
    "id": 4559,
    "post": 547,
    "parent": 0,
    "author": 0,
    "author_name": "Eve",
    "author_url": "",
    "date": "2017-07-06T05:26:52",
    "date_gmt": "2017-07-06T09:26:52",
    "content": {
      "rendered": "<p>I wanted to thank you for being so open and concise about child injury settlements in Ga.<br />\nI also thought you might want to know that the resources listed for this article are not found when i clicked the links. Do you know why that may be? I want to look more deeply into this important matter as we have reached settlement with the insurance company and after medicaid gets their requested portion back the settlement is just less than 15,000 fo my 10 year old.<br />\nImagine my surprise when I found out from my lawyers that we now need to wait for a judge to look it over and sign off. On one hand I get it.. But on the other.. Its crazy. I wasnt at fault but they didnt catch the guy so its not millions of dollars. Just uninsured medical up to 25,000.<br />\nThe car accident severely injured me and my child needs counseling to get over the trauma but was only minorly physically injured. We are lucky to have lived but I cant work now and if something doesnt happen financially soon to help us we are never going to recover no matter what. Altogether our medical bills total right a million. I am a single parent. Very very worried. Anyway.. Its not like anyone says hey theres a difference between a settlement for a kid and an adult. Thank you again for this info. I bookmarked your site. You rock.</p>\n"
    },
    "link": "https://kidinjurylaw.com/2022/07/15/legal-strategies-to-minimize-or-avoid-court-involvement-in-georgia-child-injury-settlements-part-i/#comment-4559",
