  {
    "id": 298,
    "post": 782,
    "parent": 0,
    "author": 0,
    "author_name": "shandell milliman/broussard",
    "author_url": "",
    "date": "2013-10-27T22:20:51",
    "date_gmt": "2013-10-28T02:20:51",
    "content": {
      "rendered": "<p>My autistic son was injured in sept.2013 when 3 teachers supervised by the principal forced him on the bus.he had bruises showing finger prints along with a large scratch mark. The super.says the video&#8217;s don&#8217;t show the injuries so i don&#8217;t have a case. Already the school board is protecting them while a mother in the same situation would be charged automatically. I plan to fight this all the way to the capital. I will not give up! This is only showing teachers across America they can get away with this. How in the world is this acceptable?</p>\n"
    },
